---

<BaseLayout>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="hero-status">Pre-alpha · no stable public API</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">
            Durable agent orchestration, written for Rust.
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">
            StateKnot now runs typed root Graphs through PostgreSQL crash
            recovery, atomic admission, durable model/tool attempts, lifecycle
            commits, fair scheduling, durable ingress, and verified results.
            Implemented surfaces include OpenAI/Anthropic adapters, the
            provider-native graph, AgentService v1, MCP client/OAuth/strict
            Remote Tool/Server profiles, and A2A 1.0 HTTP+JSON/JSON-RPC
            Client/Server profiles. Stable network Agent APIs, A2A gRPC, MCP
            Tasks, advanced graph semantics, Client live-peer qualification, and
            production qualification remain open.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button--primary affordance" href="/docs/"
              >Read the docs</a
            >
            <a
              class="text-link affordance"
              href="https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot"
              >Inspect source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            >
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="hero-terminal" aria-labelledby="terminal-caption">
          <figcaption id="terminal-caption">Repository validation</figcaption>
          <pre
            tabindex="0"
            aria-label="Repository validation: workspace tests and durable Graph Driver integration tests on PostgreSQL versions 16 and 17, Apache-2.0 license, pre-alpha status"><code><span class="code-muted">$</span> <span aria-hidden="true" data-type-line data-text="cargo test --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked">cargo test --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked</span>

<span class="code-muted">$</span> cargo test -p stateknot-runtime \
    --test postgres --locked

<span class="code-key">CI matrix</span>  PostgreSQL 16 / 17
<span class="code-key">License</span>    Apache-2.0
<span class="code-key">Status</span>     <span class="code-accent">pre-alpha</span></code></pre>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="section architecture-section"
      id="architecture"
      aria-labelledby="architecture-title"
    >
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="architecture-title">
          The architecture is a set of evidence boundaries.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Wire protocols stay outside the stable domain. External work stays
          outside database transactions. Recovery decisions are derived from
          bounded, integrity-checked facts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ArchitectureMap />
    </section>

    <section
      class="section current-section"
      id="current-cut"
      aria-labelledby="current-title"
    >
      <div class="section-head section-head--narrow">
        <h2 id="current-title">Current cut, without roadmap theatre.</h2>
        <p>
          “Implemented” means code exists in the pre-alpha repository. It does
          not mean the API is stable or the framework is ready for production.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="spec-head" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Surface</span>
        <span>Repository state</span>
        <span>Evidence</span>
        <span>Source</span>
      </div>
      <ul class="spec-list">
        {
          currentCut.map((item) => (
            <li class="spec-row">
              <strong>{item.surface}</strong>
              <span>{item.state}</span>
              <span>{item.evidence}</span>
              <a
                class="spec-link affordance"
                href={item.href}
                aria-label={`Inspect ${item.surface} source`}
              >
                Inspect <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section
      class="quickstart"
      id="quickstart"
      aria-labelledby="quickstart-title"
    >
      <div class="quickstart-inner">
        <div class="quickstart-copy">
          <h2 id="quickstart-title">
            Validate the repository before trusting the claims.
          </h2>
          <p>
            The facade crate is intentionally unpublished. Today’s honest
            quickstart validates the repository first, then runs a real typed
            contract example without pretending to complete the public Agent
            path.
          </p>
          <a class="dark-link affordance" href="/docs/getting-started/"
            >Open the contributor tutorial <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>

        <div class="quickstart-code">
          <div class="code-label-row">
            <span>Shell · contributor checkout</span>
            <button
              class="copy-button affordance"
              type="button"
              data-copy-button
              data-copy-target="quickstart-code"
            >
              <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <pre
            id="quickstart-code"
            tabindex="0"
            aria-label="Contributor quickstart commands"><code>git clone https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot.git
cd StateKnot
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo test --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="section roadmap-section"
      id="roadmap"
      aria-labelledby="roadmap-title"
    >
      <div class="section-head section-head--narrow">
        <h2 id="roadmap-title">The road ahead is ordered by proof.</h2>
        <p>
          The strict MCP binding retains PostgreSQL-backed recovery evidence,
          while the separate general Tool client plus OAuth provider now pass
          all 32 scored Client scenarios and the MCP Server profile passes all
          37 scored Server scenarios. The A2A 1.0 Server gate has 177 official
          TCK passes with zero failures; the Client now adds an eleven-operation
          dual-binding matrix and real PostgreSQL Unknown/no-redispatch proof.
          Live-peer qualification, reconciliation, MCP Tasks, and broader
          extensions remain independent gates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="roadmap-list">
        {
          roadmap.map((item) => (
            <li class="roadmap-item">
              <span class="roadmap-index" aria-hidden="true">
                {item.index}
              </span>
              <div>
                <h3>{item.title}</h3>
                <p>{item.body}</p>
              </div>
              <span class="roadmap-state">{item.state}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>

      <a class="text-link affordance" href="/docs/status/"
        >Open implementation status <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
      >
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
